<h2>PHORVA Documentation</h2>
<p>
PHORVA is verification infrastructure for autonomous economic activity.
It sits between autonomous agents and execution systems to determine whether
an action is authorized, consistent with intent, and correctly executed.
</p>

<h3>Core execution flow</h3>

<div class="code">AUTONOMOUS AGENT
        ↓
      INTENT
        ↓
   PHORVA CORE
        ↓
POLICY → RISK → AUTHORIZATION
        ↓
    VALIDATION
        ↓
    EXECUTION
        ↓
   VERIFICATION
        ↓
      PROOF</div>

<h3>Core concepts</h3>

<div class="docs-grid">
<div class="docs-card">
<b>Intent</b>
<p>What the agent declares it intends to execute.</p>
</div>

<div class="docs-card">
<b>Policy</b>
<p>The rules and limits that determine whether an action may proceed.</p>
</div>

<div class="docs-card">
<b>Risk</b>
<p>Transaction and execution-security analysis performed before authorization.</p>
</div>

<div class="docs-card">
<b>Authorization</b>
<p>PHORVA's decision on whether the proposed execution satisfies the required conditions.</p>
</div>

<div class="docs-card">
<b>Verification</b>
<p>Independent validation that execution matched the authorized action.</p>
</div>

<div class="docs-card">
<b>Proof-Carrying Actions</b>
<p>Execution evidence containing authorization, evaluation and verification information.</p>
</div>
</div>

<h3>Execution Graph</h3>
<p>
PHORVA can represent multi-operation executions as an execution graph,
allowing the system to verify the complete sequence and expected final state.
</p>

<div class="code">Intent
  ↓
Approve
  ↓
Swap
  ↓
Deposit
  ↓
Final State</div>

<h3>Verification evidence</h3>

<div class="code">Execution Graph
      ↓
Verification Trace
      ↓
Proof Statement
      ↓
Canonical Commitment</div>

<h3>What PHORVA is not</h3>
<ul>
<li>Not an agent wallet.</li>
<li>Not a blockchain.</li>
<li>Not a prover network.</li>
<li>Not a prover marketplace.</li>
<li>Not an agent platform.</li>
<li>Not an execution environment.</li>
<li>Not the agent's decision-maker.</li>
</ul>

<div class="docs-status">
<b>Current MVP</b>
<p>
Base Sepolia, Ethereum Sepolia and Arbitrum Sepolia testnets,
execution verification, policy enforcement, intent matching,
risk evaluation, authorization, execution graphs, final-state verification,
verification traces, proof statements, proof commitments and provider abstraction.
</p>
</div>

</div>

<h3>What PHORVA is not</h3>

<ul>
<li>Not an agent wallet.</li>
<li>Not a custody layer.</li>
<li>Not a prover marketplace.</li>
<li>Not a place where autonomous agents live.</li>
<li>Not a replacement for the agent's signer.</li>
</ul>

</div>

</div>

